#: src/positional-arguments.md:1
msgid "Positional Arguments"
msgstr ""

#: src/positional-arguments.md:3
msgid ""
"If `positional-arguments` is `true`, recipe arguments will be passed as "
"positional arguments to commands. For shell recipes, argument `$0` will be "
"the name of the recipe."
msgstr ""

#: src/positional-arguments.md:7
msgid "For example, running this recipe:"
msgstr ""

#: src/positional-arguments.md:17
msgid "Will produce the following output:"
msgstr ""

#: src/positional-arguments.md:25
msgid ""
"When using an `sh`\\-compatible shell, such as `bash` or `zsh`, `$@` expands "
"to the positional arguments given to the recipe, starting from one. When "
"used within double quotes as `\"$@\"`, arguments including whitespace will "
"be passed on as if they were double-quoted. That is, `\"$@\"` is equivalent "
"to `\"$1\" \"$2\"`… When there are no positional parameters, `\"$@\"` and "
"`$@` expand to nothing (i.e., they are removed)."
msgstr ""

#: src/positional-arguments.md:32
msgid "This example recipe will print arguments one by one on separate lines:"
msgstr ""

#: src/positional-arguments.md:34
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set positional-arguments\n"
"\n"
"@test *args='':\n"
"  bash -c 'while (( \"$#\" )); do echo - $1; shift; done' -- \"$@\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/positional-arguments.md:41
msgid "Running it with _two_ arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: src/positional-arguments.md:43
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ just test foo \"bar baz\"\n"
"- foo\n"
"- bar baz\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/positional-arguments.md:49
msgid ""
"Positional arguments may also be turned on a per-recipe basis with the "
"`[positional-arguments]` attribute<sup>1.29.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/positional-arguments.md:59
msgid ""
"Note that PowerShell does not handle positional arguments in the same way as "
"other shells, so turning on positional arguments will likely break recipes "
"that use PowerShell."
msgstr ""

#: src/positional-arguments.md:63
msgid ""
"If using PowerShell 7.4 or better, the `-CommandWithArgs` flag will make "
"positional arguments work as expected:"
msgstr ""
